EphemeralIntentExecutor_Route
├── when tokensIn are unmet
│   └── it should revert with Underfunded
├── when executed before start
│   └── it should revert with TooEarly
├── when the caller is not the keeper
│   └── it should revert with NotKeeper even for a committed route
├── when the committed route runs
│   ├── it should call the router with the committed route
│   ├── it should pass tokensIn with live balances
│   ├── it should approve tokensIn to the router for the call
│   ├── it should revoke approvals after the call
│   ├── it should pay the intent fee, not the refund fee
│   └── it should sweep remaining native to the owner
├── when a committed route carries an outcome floor
│   ├── it should enforce the floor on the committed route
│   └── it should execute once the floor clears
├── when a native tokenIn exists
│   ├── it should forward the native balance as call value
│   └── it should carry the live balance in the native entry
├── when tokenIn is an NFT
│   ├── it should pass the delivery check with the tokenId treated as ownership
│   └── it should clear the approval in the epilogue when the NFT stayed
├── when the committed NFT is absent
│   └── it should revert with Underfunded
├── when the route consumes the NFT
│   └── it should tolerate the post-move approval revoke and complete
├── when a revoke-rejecting NFT stays
│   └── it should stay strict rather than let the approval outlive the account
├── when a revoke-rejecting NFT is consumed
│   └── it should tolerate the impossible revoke once the token has moved
├── when the fee is native
│   └── it should pay the keeper in native
├── when the router call reverts
│   └── it should bubble the revert reason
├── when the fee cannot be paid
│   └── it should revert with SendFailed
└── when the fee token is codeless
    └── it should revert on the strict balance read

EphemeralIntentExecutor_Constrained
├── when the delta clears the minimum
│   ├── it should call the router with the keeper route
│   └── it should measure the delta at the recipient
├── when tokenOut is native
│   └── it should measure the native delta at the recipient
├── when any tokenOut misses its minimum
│   └── it should revert with AmountTooLow
├── when the delta is below the minimum
│   └── it should revert with AmountTooLow
├── when the route delivers to the executor instead
│   └── it should revert with AmountTooLow
├── when the outcome is a minted NFT
│   └── it should satisfy the count minimum with whatever id arrived
├── when the recipient balance decreases
│   └── it should revert with AmountTooLow, not a Panic
├── when tokensOut is empty
│   └── it should revert with Unconstrained
├── when a minimum is zero
│   └── it should revert with Unconstrained
├── when the keeper is zero
│   └── it should let any caller route against the floor and pay them the fee
└── when the caller is not the keeper
    ├── it should revert with NotKeeper
    └── it should execute for the keeper

EphemeralIntentExecutor_Refund
├── when the deadline has passed
│   ├── it should pay the refund fee best-effort, not the intent fee
│   ├── it should sweep tokensIn to the owner
│   ├── it should sweep caller-listed tokens to the owner
│   └── it should not revert on a reverting token
├── when NFTs are keeper-listed
│   └── it should sweep caller-listed NFTs to the owner
├── when the tokenIn data is malformed
│   ├── it should skip the malformed entry and complete the lifecycle
│   └── it should recover the skipped asset with a second transaction
├── when the tokenIn address word is dirty
│   └── it should truncate the dirty word and fully refund
├── when a tokenIn returns a dirty bool
│   └── it should tolerate the non-canonical return and still deliver the refund
├── when the refund recipient is zero
│   └── it should substitute the caller as beneficiary
├── when the fee token is codeless
│   └── it should skip the fee and still refund
├── when the refund fee exceeds the balance
│   └── it should skip the fee and still refund
├── when the fee token is not a tokenIn
│   ├── it should sweep the fee token remainder to the owner
│   └── it should pay nothing on a repeated refund
├── when the refund fee is native
│   └── it should pay the keeper before the selfdestruct sweep
├── when a refund is permissionless
│   └── it should let any caller refund and earn the refund fee
└── when executed on the wrong chain
    ├── it should sweep immediately without waiting for the gates
    └── it should sweep native via selfdestruct

EphemeralIntentExecutor_Owner
├── when the owner calls without a route
│   ├── it should refund tokensIn before the deadline
│   ├── it should pay no fee
│   ├── it should not call the router
│   └── it should sweep native via selfdestruct
├── when the owner calls before start
│   └── it should refund without waiting for the start gate
├── when the owner calls on a keeper-routed intent
│   ├── it should refund rather than wait for the keeper
│   └── it should leave the keeper nothing to execute
├── when the owner lists extra tokens
│   ├── it should sweep them alongside tokensIn
│   └── it should tolerate a listed tokenIn
├── when the owner submits a route
│   ├── it should call the router with the owner's bytes, not the committed route
│   ├── it should pass tokensIn with live balances
│   ├── it should not take a fee off the top
│   ├── it should revoke approvals after the call
│   ├── it should sweep remaining native to the owner
│   └── it should leave route residue recoverable by an owner refund
├── when the owner submits a route under closed gates
│   └── it should execute without the start, tokensIn, keeper, or outcome gates
├── when the owner submits a route outside the window
│   └── it should route rather than refund
├── when the owner route reverts
│   ├── it should bubble the revert reason
│   └── it should leave the refund arm available
├── when the keeper is zero and a third party submits a route
│   ├── it should ignore the bytes and run the committed route
│   └── it should pay the caller the intent fee
└── when the owner is zero and a keeper submits a route
    └── it should not grant the keeper owner privileges
